, middle, caudal, and accessory lobes, and a tracheal bronchus supplies the cranial lobe; human lobation and branching differ."]],["ARTICLE",{"__playwright_target__":"call@22","class":"diss-comparison-card","data-comparison-specimen":"perch","data-current":"false"},[[24,953]],["H4",{},"Gills"],[[24,957]],["DIV",{"data-gas-comparison":"perch"},["FIGURE",{"class":"diss-pump-diagram","data-gas-diagram":"perch"},["svg",{"viewBox":"0 0 300 178","role":"img","aria-label":"Perch gill concept: water flows one way and blood the opposite way at thin lamellae. They remain separated by the exchange barrier.","focusable":"false"},["text",{"x":"150","y":"22","text-anchor":"middle"},"Water flow →"],["path",{"d":"M34 40 H267 M258 34 L267 40 L258 46","fill":"none","stroke":"#286574","stroke-width":"3","stroke-linecap":"round","stroke-linejoin":"round"}],["rect",{"x":"94","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"113","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"132","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"151","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"170","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"189","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"208","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["rect",{"x":"227","y":"62","width":"9","height":"42","rx":"3","fill":"#e2f1f2","stroke":"#416277","stroke-width":"1.5"}],["text",{"x":"150","y":"83","text-anchor":"middle"}],["text",{"x":"150","y":"123","text-anchor":"middle"},"Thin lamellae"],["path",{"d":"M267 142 H34 M43 136 L34 142 L43 148","